Error [jet.CopyNotSupported]: `Res?` can't be copied out of the place it is read from
  --> tests/ui/resource_forwarded_out_of_place.jet:20:10
    |
 20 |     r: h.first ?? return 0
    |          ^^^^^
 Why: It holds a resource, which has one cleanup owner; this position takes an owned value, so the copy and the place would both close the same resource
 Fix: Use it where it is, or take `h` as a `&&` parameter or receiver and move the field out with `.move()`
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0211

Error [jet.MissingMoveMarker]: `env` cannot be moved from borrowed storage
  --> tests/ui/resource_forwarded_out_of_place.jet:25:8
    |
 25 |     r: env ?? return 0
    |        ^^^
 Why: `env` is a read or write parameter, so its caller keeps the value, and `Res?` can't be copied into an owned value
 Fix: Declare the parameter `env: &&Res?` so the caller hands the value over
More: jet-lang.dev/e/E0201

